storical metadata-only reader behavior.\n- `context-item.test.ts:193-275`: current sorting and `assembleUserContent()` tests describe replay behavior that layer 2 removes.\n- `context-item-producers.test.ts`: currently has no complete-envelope/final-text assertions for model switch, availability, digest, and temporal factories. This is the direct dependency from tasks 2.2.1–2.2.2.\n- `context-item-temporal.test.ts:75-87,100-224`: update factory and replay expectations to persisted final text; retain payload validation and exactly-one-temporal coverage.\n- `chat-loop-binding.integration.test.ts:770-800`: currently proves filtering of old `data-model-context` plus reasoning, but not `data-context`, reserved delimiter sanitation, multiple text-part boundaries, or stored order.\n- `chat-loop-binding.integration.test.ts:802-963`: producer expectations are metadata-only; update to complete `data.text` and assert canonical order.\n- `chat-loop.integration.test.ts:761-869`: already verifies message/snapshot/Run/event rollback together when `run.created` fails. Retain it and add exact canonical-part assertions.\n- `chat-loop.integration.test.ts:916-1032`: currently checks temporal and old metadata-only parts; update expected shapes and add multipart sanitation.\n- `chats-messages.integration.test.ts:365-422`: only submits one plain text part; add HTTP coverage for multiple reserved-delimiter text parts and persistence.\n- `run-execution-tools.integration.test.ts:1841-2005`: currently derives expected receipt/provider text via `renderContextItemPart()`; update to `switchPart.data.text`.\n- `apps/api/src/testing/support.ts:496-539`: already asserts exactly one temporal row and target Run ID. Preserve this helper.\n\n## Commands/checks\n\n- `git status --short --branch` initially: clean `rendered-context/context-parts`; later showed the other worker’s files listed above.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- `pnpm --filter api exec vitest run --project unit src/chats/dto/chats.dto.